("p", "Capability one: certified large-deviation telemetry for monitored quantum circuits. The exact closure turns the ESS law — ESS/B = exp[−2Lt·(Λ(2)−2Λ(1))] — from a warning into an engineering budget curve: at p = 0.16 the exponent is 0.0340 nats per site at L = 8, and the true ESS fractions are 2.7 × 10<super>−8</super>, 3.6 × 10<super>−18</super>, 4.2 × 10<super>−32</super> at L = 8, 12, 16, so any fixed sampling budget fails at a computable system size, and the computation is exact. The self-averaging criterion — the per-site variance of the record count, 0.104–0.106, L-independent — is the sampling certificate that says when a single disorder realization speaks for the ensemble; the record-entropy density ladder (0.1448 to 0.1489 bits per site) is the telemetry channel itself. The protocol: run the monitor, report the record exponents with exact-arithmetic certificates attached, flag the record-phase boundaries by the certified p-locations. This is the first capability in the quantum corpus that an experimentalist could operate without reading the theory, because every number it reports is either exact or carries its own error contract."),
("p", "Capability two: the obstruction spectrometer (Theorem V’s protocol, with its calibration table). Capability three: curvature-guided intervention design. The design rule falls directly out of Theorem IV’s proved metabolic half: interventions placed at curvature atoms — the non-analytic boundaries where second-order response concentrates — buy maximal response per unit cost, because the value–flux coupling identity fixes the exact exchange rate there, and the epistasis structure (ρ<sub>S</sub> = 0.865 between curvature epistasis and footprint overlap) supplies the interaction bookkeeping. The sustainability corpus supplies the calibrated instances: the COD intervention analysis returns a largest robust constant catch of 91.6 kt and a certified-kernel horizon of seven years at the limit reference point; the Edwards analysis returns a smallest securing cut of 7.2 percent against a 618-ft threshold; and — the negative instance that proves the rule — the reactive rules that are “invisible to the kernels of their own triggers” are interventions placed off the concentration set, failing silently exactly where the curvature is not. The frozen-protocol forecast ladders are the falsification harness, and Prediction 9 states the dominance test."),
("p", "Capability four: dual-certified policy bands — machine-checkable governance. The minimax dual certificate theorem says the common safe-action set is empty precisely when an adversarial probability measure on the boundary–disturbance bundle drives expected inward drift negative against every control, with support of at most k+1 points, tight; the computational certification bridge turns it into a finite linear program whose optimum brackets the continuous-time safety value from both sides with certified error inflation. Assembled, these are policy proofs: a policy certificate is a small rational object — a measure with at most k+1 atoms, an exact margin (the benchmark instance certifies obstruction at Y = 6 with margin 3/50 on the two-stock problem whose critical aggregate is exactly 27/5) — that any third party can verify without re-solving anything, in the exact arithmetic the corpus already practices. This is the sustainability corpus’s answer to its own reception risk: not more models, but certificates that travel. Capability five, stated briefly because the chess paper already carries it: role-decomposed theory engines. The CSR sufficiency theorem and the amplification bound P ≥ [θ(1−(1−q)<super>w</super>)]<super>L</super> are substrate-independent; the corpus’s own arena agents are running instances; and the society architecture — generator, critics, verifier, attacker, coordinator — is the operational form of this volume’s own discipline of separating the proved from the conjectured."),
